## Procedural office materials

- Character pixels and state frames: local pixel-art.ts algorithms and arrays; generated in memory as Pixi RenderTextures by textures.ts. No source image.
- Floor, windows and selection: local scene.ts Graphics geometry; cached in memory as textures. No source image.
- Desk, chair, monitor, keyboard and shadows: vendored MIT DeskEntity procedural Graphics fallback (classic artwork); in-memory texture caching. No original PNG loaded.
- Whiteboard: vendored MIT propViews Graphics geometry, with local meeting text; in-memory texture caching. No source image.
- Labels: operating-system system-ui/sans-serif fonts already available on the host. No font files are bundled or downloaded for the office.

Local procedural integration code follows this repository's MIT license. Generated textures live only in the local renderer/GPU and are explicitly released with their owner; they are not downloaded assets or binary image files in the distribution.

The bundled renderer does not ship node_modules. The directly used office dependencies are attributed below. Existing application dependency notices remain in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt in the packaged renderer; the engine license remains in resources/HEART-PORTAL-LICENSE.

